A||||9||mrgone||85 & 86 model differences||||1||
Z||000000||mrgone||08-10-2001||02:23 AM||||ok my favourite fiero is the notchback with gt bumpers, v6.<P>85 gt and 86 se...<P>im thinking the most obvious difference would be the steering wheel, the DOT 3rd brake light on the 86..<P>but what are the real differences? what makes the 85 a GT and the 86 an SE?<BR>or did the gt name just get bumped up to the fastback because it was the new model. leaving near no difference between the two.<P>or did i answer my own question. damn<P>whats the diff       85 gt and 86 se?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||08-10-2001||02:59 AM||||Differences are:<BR>(Difference - Year)<BR>Third brake light - 86<BR>Backlit gauges - 86<BR>Aux Gauges above radio pod - 86<BR>Sail panel speakers - 86<BR>Seat speakers - 85<BR>Base engine is 2.5L 4-cyl - 86<BR>V-6 with 5-spd - Late 86<BR>Subwoofer option - 86<BR>Silver aero skirt - 85<BR>Black aero skirt - 86<BR>4-spoke steering wheel - 86<P>That's all I can think of, I may have missed something.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Kelvin Vivian||08-10-2001||03:02 AM||||I too wonder what the differences are between a 1985 GT and a 1986 2M6... I would think that with the exception of the third brake light and steering wheel, the two cars would be mechanically identical.<P>Edited due to Orief's posting.... Ah, now I sees some differences....<P>Perhaps Pontiac revised the suspension for 1986 a bit. I think they were always tweeking the suspension between each of the model years.<P>Fieros with the aero/notchback look, and factory dual twin exhaust pipes w/production numbers:<P>1984 Indy Fiero ~ 2000 <BR>1985 GT         ~ 22,539 <BR>1986 SE 2M4     ~ 4,031<BR>1986 SE 2M6     ~ 28,274<BR>1987 SE 4-cyl   ~ 1,401<BR>1987 SE V6      ~ 2,474<P>For 1987 the "2M4/6" designations were dropped.<p>[This message has been edited by Kelvin Vivian (edited 08-10-2001).]||||reg||3
Z||000003||Uaana||08-10-2001||04:24 AM||||Question about the 2M4/6 designations. <BR>I've seen a couple of Fieros badges simply as a Fiero mine included and it's an 85 SE 6cyl. My previous 85 showed 2m4 and was also a SE. <BR>So why the difference?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Hank is Here||08-10-2001||05:37 AM||||Heaedlight motors????||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||08-10-2001||05:45 AM||||Hank--Headlight motors didn't change until '87.<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000006||AusFiero||08-10-2001||09:29 AM||||Oreif. Black aero trim 86? Was than an option? I have a late 86 GT Fastback 5 speed and before they was resprayed red the aero trims was definately silver. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||5
Z||000007||Hartz||08-10-2001||10:06 AM||||Aus - 86/87 aero nose notchbacks - SE's - had sort of a matte black aero package, where the fastbacks were silver.  As far as I know, color was the only difference of these parts.<P>Hartz<BR>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo||||reg||1
Z||000008||Oreif||08-10-2001||10:35 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AusFiero:<BR><B>Oreif. Black aero trim 86? Was than an option? I have a late 86 GT Fastback 5 speed and before they was resprayed red the aero trims was definately silver. <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>These are the differences between the 85 GT and 86 SE. <BR>All GT's (85 thru 87)(and 84 Indy's) used the silver trim and 86-87 SE's had black.||||reg||1
Z||000009||JJ-85-2M6||08-10-2001||10:06 PM||||The 1985 SE came from the factory with the "Fiero 2M4" or "Fiero 2M6" sticker.  Maybe someone replaced yours with the wrong sticker. Later models just had the word "Fiero"  I believe that started with the 1987 or 1988 model.  J||||reg||10
